    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d732">

                <pb facs="0835" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg825"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10–3148: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)<anchor n="30" xml:id="d732-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-01T16:00:00-05:00">November 1, 1948—4
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1519. Re Mukden’s 457 [<hi rendition="#italic">456</hi>] Oct 31,<anchor n="31"
                        xml:id="d732-f2"/> rptd Nanking as 606. Emb authorized in its discretion
                    approach Chinese authorities and ask whether CAF plans bomb Mukden. If reply
                    negative inform Chinese you will so inform your Govt. If reply affirmative, Emb
                    should point out sites Mukden where Americans located and express hope that any
                    possible post-surrender bombing of Mukden be carefully limited to targets of
                    military significance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d732-f1" n="30" type="source" xml:id="d732-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated as telegram No. 192, November 3, to the Consul General at Mukden.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d732-f2" n="31" xml:id="d732-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg530">p. 530</ref>. Mukden was
                    occupied by Chinese Communist forces on November 1.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
